> A conditional error model, not a posterior probability

For a fixed odd non-Carmichael composite, the coprime passing residues
form a proper subgroup of the unit group. Its size is at most half the
unit-group size. Removing always-passing endpoints does not increase that
fraction. With independent uniform draws from a specified population with
passing fraction f, all k rounds pass with probability f^k. Carmichael
numbers have f=1 under conditioning on coprimality, so that conditioned
model has no decreasing bound. On the unconditioned sampler support,
noncoprime witnesses make f smaller. These statements concern a fixed
composite under an ideal draw model; f^k is not the probability that an
input is composite given a pass. The native deterministic stream has no
such iid guarantee. See Shoup, Theorem10.1 and the following discussion.

The plotted curves use actual census numerators/denominators but then
apply this hypothetical iid model. They are neither observed frequencies
from the native generator nor a security claim. Native same-base
Miller–Rabin checks are included as a stronger comparison; they do not
change the Fermat algorithm being studied.

Optional trace history stores C=completed_rounds whole records. Default
quota1000000 and the requested round count are independent; zero quota
argument disables only capture quota. A record is admitted before its
draw/gcd/power, and failures return no partial trace. Metadata, vector
capacity, allocators and runtime storage are excluded from C: it is not
peak memory. Work calls use constant auxiliary storage and no history
quota. Copies own their rows independently.

A round uses O(log(n)) modular products for this fixed-width representation,
plus a gcd. R actual rounds take O(R log(n)) word work and a trace keeps
O(R) records. An exhaustive B-base census takes O(B log(n)) word work,
constant storage, and a default one-million-base work cap checked before
any test. Arbitrary-precision bit costs differ. These routines expose
branches and values and are educational numerical APIs, not constant-time
cryptographic primitives.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fermat_primality_limits.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/algorithms/primality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory_extra.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/miller_rabin.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <cstdint>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto c=dm::algorithms::fermat_base_census(561,2,560);const double conditional=double(c.passes)/c.coprime,unconditional=double(c.passes)/c.total;std::vector<double>x,unit,all;std::print("| hypothetical iid rounds k | coprime-conditioned 561 pass probability | uniform-support 561 pass probability |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");for(int k:{1,2,4,8,16,20}){x.push_back(k);unit.push_back(std::pow(conditional,k));all.push_back(std::pow(unconditional,k));std::print("| {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",k,unit.back(),all.back());}
  std::print("\n| n | base | Fermat passes | same-base strong probable-prime passes |\n| ---: | ---: | :--- | :--- |\n");for(const auto& pair:std::vector<std::pair<std::uint64_t,std::uint64_t>>{{97,2},{341,2},{561,2},{1105,2}}){const auto r=dm::algorithms::fermat_base_test(pair.first,pair.second);std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",pair.first,pair.second,r.passes,dm::algorithms::is_strong_probable_prime_base(pair.first,pair.second));}
  bool trace_cap=false,census_cap=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::fermat_probable_prime_trace(97,3,0,2);}catch(const std::length_error&){trace_cap=true;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::fermat_base_census(561,1,561,559);}catch(const std::length_error&){census_cap=true;}const auto exact=dm::algorithms::fermat_probable_prime_trace(97,3,0,3),off=dm::algorithms::fermat_probable_prime_trace(97,3,0,0);auto edited=exact;const auto owned=edited;edited.rows.front().base=0;std::print("\nCapture controls: too-small quota rejects {}; exact quota {}; disabled quota {}; owned first base {}; edited first base {}.\n",trace_cap,exact.captured_entries,off.captured_entries,owned.rows.front().base,edited.rows.front().base);std::print("Census controls: too-small work cap rejects {}; empty interval total {}.\n",census_cap,dm::algorithms::fermat_base_census(561,561,561).total);
  int invalid=0;try{(void)dm::algorithms::fermat_probable_prime(9,0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::fermat_base_test(7,7);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::fermat_base_census(7,4,3);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}std::print("Invalid zero-round/base/interval controls rejected {}/3.\n",invalid);
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.line(x,unit,"Coprime only",{220,38,38},2).points(x,unit,"",{220,38,38},5).line(x,all,"Uniform support",{37,99,235},2).points(x,all,"",{37,99,235},5).title("561 under a hypothetical independent uniform model").x_label("Hypothetical rounds k").y_label("Model probability that all k rounds pass").y_limits(0,1.15).size(1100,560).save_svg("build/fermat_primality_limits.svg");if(!trace_cap||!census_cap||invalid!=3||owned.rows.front().base==0)throw std::runtime_error("limit controls failed");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
